    "findings": [
      "Hunyuan3D text2image appends asset background/style/quality terms and supplies a negative prompt covering anatomy, proportions, missing/extra limbs, fused digits and long necks. This is its text-to-image stage, not a GPT modeling-code system prompt.",
      "Hunyuan3D multiview preprocessing tags and orders front,left,back,right explicitly; ComfyUI multiview conditioning preserves semantic view identities through position embeddings.",
      "ComfyUI core CLIPTextEncode tokenizes user text; Hunyuan3D shape conditioning uses vision embeddings and zero negative embeddings. Core nodes do not automatically inject universal anatomy instructions.",
      "ComfyUI emphasis and dynamic-prompt syntax depends on diffusion encoder/frontend; it is not a GPT structured-plan weighting API."
    ],
    "adaptation": [
      "Preserve complete user subject and explicit requested style; never port HunyuanDiT sixty-character truncation or force cartoon style.",
      "Condition human-only positive anatomy targets and explicit negative failure criteria; do not apply human digit/limb counts to organic nonhumans.",
      "Require coherent view labels and shared geometry; unspecified viewpoints remain unknown rather than silently assuming front.",
      "Use one ChatGPT-authenticated CLI plan call and fixed trusted local interpreter; do not load ComfyUI or neural 3D weights."
    ],
